 Sounds good. I hope you get much joy from sinking into this marvellous civilization. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:06:41-08:00","id":64247,"title":"","content":"I've always loved Ancient Sumer for a long time. It's one of the reasons I want to develop the Ancient Hunting Grounds from the barebones we have, and turn it into a full setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:51:52-08:00","id":64470,"title":"","content":"Ahah! Found it <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaulta07d-4.html?g=posts&amp;t=72914\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/d...=posts&amp;t=72914</a> By Omicron. Not a lot I can really use, but in that vein. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T21:31:31-08:00","id":64577,"title":"","content":"Alright, my first thought is that the Tribes are literally tribes. A werewolf is born into a Tribe. They take the tribe of their werewolf parent. I imagine they work like houses and a king, or<i> Ur-luhal</i>, is chosen among the alphas of the packs from the tribes. That's the basic of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T07:25:46-08:00","id":64822,"title":"","content":"<i>This story is true.<br /> Before the sundering of creation, before the veil was raised, Pangaea was bound to the whims of the Celestine. Anulal, called by mortals as Anu, the lord of the firmament brought the stars, and ephemera to existence; Akihana whose heart brought life and structure where otherwise none could flourish; and Iduth-Nanna, the mother moon, the eternal lover of the Earth whose reflection gave insight to a place of eternal chaos.<br /> <br /> Through these greater spirits was the world born, and under their watchful eyes did all things rise and fall in harmony with each other. Yet as all things that begin must end, so too ruin did befall the peace of Pangaea, with the coming of Gurimirska.<br /> <br /> Gurimirska, called by the mortals as Tiamat, the Primordial Dragon. When he appeared from the ancient places below, so too he did bring catastrophe. To what end, none but the Celestines could say, for he choked the world in corruption and wrapped Akihana in his deadly coils. With fury did the host of Gurimirska assault the world.<br /> <br /> For then did Anulal call upon the gods of the Earth, and they did war upon the brood of Gurimirska. It was child of Iduth-Nanna, and Akihana that finally slew Gurimirska the serpent of the depths, and progenitor of monsters. Cunning Enlil had a plan to battle the fearsome primordial beast. It was Ur-Farah, protector of the Earth. With the strength of Ur-Farah and the spear of Enlil, was Gurimirska torn asunder. Enlil, called El, was crowned King of Earth. Ur-Farah took no gifts, for he only sought to protect his mother.<br /> <br /> And lo, did man, the animal upraised by Enlil, spread through out the earth. He did worship the gods, minor and great, an appeased them with burnt offerings. Enlil taught them society and they built like their god's. Iduth-Nanna was worshiped in these ancient times, and so did she deign to use the new animal to ease the burden of her beloved Ur-Farah. The high priestess of Iduth-Nanna, called Bau, was given eight children with the seed of Ur-Farah, from their do the People spring.<br /> <br /> Iduth-Nana gave us the ability to assume new forms between human and wolf, matching her auspices. Akihana extended our abilities to track and hunt, and gave us the basic foundation of our society \u2014 pack and territory. Both taught us the ways of the spirit world. The Lunes and elementals guided our path and rewarded our victories. Harsh Luna exacted a ban upon us for her gifts \u2014 the touch of her metal, silver, would burn us. Akihana, the earth mother, bid us to keep her world and its Shadow in balance. To do this, Akihana gave us the right to prey upon human and spirit to keep the worlds in balance.<br /> <br /> We became powerful shamans who knew how to walk with one foot in both worlds \u2014 one in light, the other in Shadow. We were kings of the primordial wood. None could out-fight, out-think or out-magic us. We kept the wolves in check, and we kept the villages of humans small and isolated.<br /> <br /> It was then that Iduth-Nanna bade us to protect nascent humanity. We were to shepherd them from their prideful state, and keep them from ravaging the world. We were forbid to hunt them for their flesh any longer. So, the eight children and the tribes of Ur-Farah convened. This new commandment was debated, for six days, and seven nights. On the morning of the seventh day a vote was held. Five of the eight voted that them and their tribe would uphold the commandment of Iduth-Nanna, the other three grew angry. They said that humanity would harm the mother Akihana. They named themselves the Pure and left, vowing to be enemies of humanity and their protectors, the Ur-Sag.<br /> <br /> To this day, we protect humanity, and rule them as divine kings. Territory is held, and we keep the spirits in line. As Iduth-Nanna bade, we follow and prosper. This is the legacy of Bau.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""